docs-truth.docNotes:
My docs changes describe the code at base f5c0328 plus my own group's changes. The orchestrator's final dated section needs to cover the following.

(1) For each 21.10 owner decision in ACCEPTANCE «Current state → League owner decisions», state whether and from which commit the code implements it. The decisions are worded as rules:
- shared player credited to the first holder only, later buyer's slot 0, both teams kept for purchases in the same window;
- 1st-place and top-3 Monte Carlo probabilities in the standings;
- ESPN/model games mean (projection-inputs);
- EXACT_MINUTES participation (no code change needed).

(2) If projection-model or projection-inputs change the model, refresh every number in the «Current state» holdout and slot-value bullets from the new public/data/projection-model-audit.json. Today they are:
- 484 players; season MAE 250 vs 275; gain 13.6–36.7; FP/game 2.53 vs 2.69; games 17.1 vs 18.9;
- 74.6% inside the range, 10.3% below, 15.1% above; floor 24%; Brier 0.133 vs 0.158; games range 79.8%;
- healthy start 13.4 vs 14.1, bias −0.7 vs −4.2;
- Spearman 0.64 vs 0.55; slot MAE 185 vs 320; top-40 +0.4% (58,770 vs 58,549); top-80 +1.2% (108,294 vs 106,970); replaced games 20.3 vs 23.2;
- teammate correlation −0.2% over 16,673 pairs.

tests/test_docs_truth.py checks these against public/data when it is present.

(3) The in-season bullet (2.34→2.28, 2.84→2.68, 0.224→0.190) must change with data/inseason-calibration.json; tests/test_docs_truth.py enforces this.

(4) After the ESPN games mean, the «Current state» figure 'ESPN 67.4 vs model 58.5 (+8.9)' still describes the inputs. The shipped games then sit about halfway, at a mean of about 63.0 for those 313 players. Say so.

(5) ACCEPTANCE:142 says 'Moves are advised from 70%'. Confirm that the season-transfers fix makes the hero card follow it; at base it says «Сделай» from 60%. If season-transfers recalibrates the confidence, replace the «not backtested» line in «Current state» with its measured calibration.

(6) If the season-availability or season-transfers verdict band changes, update line 111 ('a season gain of 15+ decides first; a smaller season gain with a month loss of 15+ is still weakening').

(7) Sports.ru history numbers (98 of 417 flagged, 79 flips, 58 of 346 trend changes) are from the 20.10 database and will move slightly with new forecasts. They are dated as such.

(8) The external scoring check figures (387 / 151 / 318 / +1.2 / 35.7) depend only on repo data and will not change unless the logs or the Sports.ru history change.

draft-engine.crossGroupNotes:
1) REQUIRED, scripts/e2e-smoke.mjs (no owning group). Without this change the CI 'Browser smoke test' step in pages.yml fails: a fresh browser context now gets the official draft in LIVE mode, so #draft-desk is hidden and #rookies-only.check() times out. Replace the two lines
 await page.getByRole('button',{name:'Драфт'}).first().click();await page.waitForTimeout(2000);
 await page.locator('#rookies-only').check();await page.waitForTimeout(1500);
with
 await page.getByRole('button',{name:'Драфт'}).first().click();await page.waitForTimeout(2000);
 // After 18.10 the real draft is the official one: the tab shows its results, not the pick desk.
 assert.match(await page.locator('#postdraft').innerText(),/Итоги драфта/i);assert.equal(await page.locator('.team-roster').count(),8);
 assert.ok(await page.locator('#draft-desk').isHidden(),'no pick desk for the finished real draft');
 // The rookie filter and the player cards are exercised in training mode.
 await page.locator('#settings > summary').click();await page.selectOption('#draft-mode','INTERACTIVE');await page.waitForTimeout(2000);
 await page.locator('#rookies-only').check();await page.waitForTimeout(1500);
The /i flag is needed because the eyebrow is uppercased by CSS. I verified this exact patch locally (passes).
2) Optional, src/main.js renderStatus (outside my scope): 'добор от' still calls completionPlan(t) without the white list. For our team it could call completionPlan(t,team,{white:whiteFor(team)}) to match the gate. whiteFor is defined near the top of main.js.
3) Optional, src/analysis.js (no group): recommendations use pickCompletion(state,id) without white, so for our team they may list a pick the card gate then refuses on the white rule. Fix: pass the white list for team 0.
4) season-ui group (main.js render/seasonCatalog, new src/standings.js): randomFromSeed now scrambles its seed, so any seeded Monte Carlo built on it gives different (still deterministic) numbers; pinned exact values must be re-derived. Fresh LIVE devices now hold 80 picks whose snapshots equal the installed catalog, so seasonCatalog is unaffected.
5) season-ui/docs-truth (src/insights.js): the F143 'Недооценён рынком' gap for ESPN ADP ≥130 was not changed here. That file is not mine.
6) main.js merge: my edits are in the WHITE/whiteFor block at the top, setMode plus the new seedLive, chooseReplacement, choose, cardAction, loadDatabase (two seedLive() calls), the reset handler, and one text in renderPlan's 'Как считается' note (survival-odds label). I did not touch render(), forecastSources, forecastCard or the season wiring.
